        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 4 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 2 days\n**Started**: 2026-03-02\n\n## Overview\n\nA lightweight, zero-dependency CLI tool that validates YAML file syntax. Consists of two modules in a flat `src/` directory: a custom YAML parser (`yaml-parser.ts`) that performs line-by-line syntax validation for a defined YAML subset, and a CLI entry point (`validate-yaml.ts`) that handles file I/O, argument parsing, output formatting, and exit codes. Runnable via `bun run validate <file>`.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Core parser module; no dependencies on other new code\n2. [T2, T3] - T2 tests T1 (interface dependency); T3 imports T1 (interface dependency); T2 and T3 are independent of each other\n3. [T4] - CLI tests depend on T3 being implemented\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: T2 imports parseYaml from T1)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: T3 imports parseYaml from T1)\n- T4 -> T3 (Build: T4 tests the CLI entry point T3 provides)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T3 -> T4\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Core Parser (Group 1)\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Implement YAML parser module (`src/yaml-parser.ts`) with line-by-line syntax validation, indentation stack tracking, key-value and list item validation, comment handling, and quoted string recognition `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-yaml-parser-module-srcyaml-parserts](design.md#31-yaml-parser-module-srcyaml-parserts)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/yaml-parser.ts` exports `ParseResult` interface with `valid: boolean` and optional `error: { message: string; line: number }`\n    - [ ] File `src/yaml-parser.ts` exports `parseYaml(content: string): ParseResult` function\n    - [ ] Empty content (zero-length or whitespace-only) returns `{ valid: true }`\n    - [ ] Comment-only lines (optional whitespace followed by `#`) are skipped during parsing\n    - [ ] Blank lines (whitespace-only) are skipped during parsing\n    - [ ] Tab characters in leading whitespace produce an error result with descriptive message and line number\n    - [ ] Indentation stack tracks allowed indent levels starting with `[0]`, pushes on deeper indent, pops on dedent, and errors on inconsistent dedent to non-matching level\n    - [ ] Key-value pairs matching `<key>: <value>` or `<key>:` (for nested blocks) are recognized as valid\n    - [ ] List items matching `- <value>` pattern at current indent are recognized as valid\n    - [ ] Inline comments (` #` preceded by a space, not inside quoted strings) are stripped before line validation\n    - [ ] Quoted strings (single and double) are recognized to prevent false positives on special characters within quotes\n    - [ ] Lines that are neither key-value pairs, list items, nor contextual continuations produce a syntax error with line number\n    - [ ] No external dependencies are imported; only built-in modules are used\n\n### Parser Tests and CLI Entry Point (Group 2)\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Write comprehensive parser unit tests (`src/yaml-parser.test.ts`) covering valid files, invalid files, and edge cases including empty input, comments-only, nesting, indentation errors, inline comments, quoted strings, and tab detection `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#parser-unit-tests-srcyaml-parsertestts](design.md#parser-unit-tests-srcyaml-parsertestts)\n\n    **Effort**: 5 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Test file `src/yaml-parser.test.ts` exists and uses `bun:test` framework\n    - [ ] Tests cover valid cases: empty file, whitespace-only file, comment-only file, simple key-value, multiple key-values, simple list, nested mapping, nested list under key, deep nesting, inline comments, boolean values, null value, key with colon in value, quoted string value, key with empty value (trailing colon), dedent to previous valid level\n    - [ ] Tests cover invalid cases: inconsistent indentation, missing colon (bare words), tab indentation, dedent to invalid level\n    - [ ] Each test asserts on the `valid` field and, for invalid cases, asserts the `error` object contains a meaningful `message` and correct `line` number\n    - [ ] All tests pass when run via `bun test`\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Implement CLI entry point (`src/validate-yaml.ts`) with argument parsing, file reading with error handling, output formatting to stdout/stderr, exit code management (0=valid, 1=invalid, 2=operational error), and add `\"validate\"` script to `package.json` `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-cli-entry-point-srcvalidate-yamlts](design.md#32-cli-entry-point-srcvalidate-yamlts)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/validate-yaml.ts` exists and imports `parseYaml` from `./yaml-parser.ts`\n    - [ ] Missing file path argument outputs `\"Usage: bun run validate <file>\"` to stderr and exits with code 2\n    - [ ] File not found (ENOENT) outputs `\"Error: File not found: <path>\"` to stderr and exits with code 2\n    - [ ] File not readable (EACCES) outputs `\"Error: Cannot read file: <path>\"` to stderr and exits with code 2\n    - [ ] Other file read errors output `\"Error: <message>\"` to stderr and exit with code 2\n    - [ ] Valid YAML file outputs `\"<path> is valid\"` to stdout and exits with code 0\n    - [ ] Invalid YAML file outputs `\"<path> is invalid: <error.message> (line <error.line>)\"` to stderr and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] File reading uses `readFileSync` with `\"utf-8\"` encoding from `node:fs`\n    - [ ] `package.json` contains script entry `\"validate\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"`\n    - [ ] No external dependencies are imported; only built-in modules (`node:fs`, `node:path`) and local `yaml-parser.ts` are used\n\n### CLI Integration Tests (Group 3)\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Write CL