        "content": "# Feature Verification Report #1\n\n**Generated**: 2026-03-02T09:10:00Z\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Verification Scope**: all\n**KB Context**: -- Not loaded (context directory does not exist; consider running /knowledge-build)\n**Field Notes**: -- Not available (no field-notes.md found in feature directory)\n\n## Executive Summary\n- Overall Status: VERIFIED\n- Acceptance Criteria: 22/22 verified (100%)\n- Implementation Quality: HIGH\n- Ready for Merge: YES\n\nAll 22 acceptance criteria across 7 functional requirements have been verified through code examination and live functional testing. The implementation faithfully follows the design specification, uses zero external dependencies, and all 39 tests (32 parser unit tests + 5 CLI integration tests + 2 pre-existing utility tests) pass. Exit codes, output formatting, error handling, and the parser logic all conform to the documented requirements.\n\n## Field Notes Context\n**Field Notes Available**: -- No\n\n### Documented Deviations\nNo field notes file exists for this feature. The tasks.md file documents one deviation: T1 added a `prevAllowsNesting` guard to prevent deeper indentation after lines with inline values (e.g., `key: value` cannot have children). This was implied by test expectations but not explicitly present in the design algorithm pseudocode. The deviation is reasonable and does not conflict with any acceptance criterion.\n\n### Undocumented Deviations\nNone found. The implementation closely follows the design specification across all components.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Verification\n\n### FR-001: File Path Input\n**AC-001.1**: The command accepts exactly one positional argument representing a file path.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/validate-yaml.ts`:5 - `const filePath = process.argv[2]`\n- Evidence: The CLI reads `process.argv[2]` as the file path argument. Functional testing confirms `bun run validate /tmp/test_valid.yaml` correctly accepts the path and validates the file.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-001.2**: If no argument is provided, the command outputs a usage message to stderr and exits with a non-zero exit code.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/validate-yaml.ts`:7-10 - `if (!filePath) { process.stderr.write(\"Usage: bun run validate <file>\\n\"); process.exit(2); }`\n- Evidence: Functional test confirms running `bun run validate` with no args outputs \"Usage: bun run validate <file>\" to stderr and exits with code 2. CLI integration test at `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/validate-yaml.test.ts`:35-40 also verifies this.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-001.3**: If more than one argument is provided, the command uses the first argument as the file path (remaining arguments are ignored).\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/validate-yaml.ts`:5 - `const filePath = process.argv[2]`\n- Evidence: By reading only `process.argv[2]`, any additional arguments at `process.argv[3+]` are naturally ignored. Functional test confirmed: `bun run validate /tmp/test_valid.yaml extra_arg1 extra_arg2` produces valid output and exit code 0.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-002: File Access Validation\n**AC-002.1**: If the file does not exist, the command outputs an error message indicating the file was not found and exits with a distinct non-zero exit code.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/validate-yaml.ts`:19-20 - `if (error.code === \"ENOENT\") { process.stderr.write(\"Error: File not found: ${filePath}\\n\"); }`\n- Evidence: Functional test with `/nonexistent/file.yaml` outputs \"Error: File not found: /nonexistent/file.yaml\" and exits with code 2. CLI integration test at `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/validate-yaml.test.ts`:42-47 also verifies this.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-002.2**: If the file cannot be read (permissions issue), the command outputs an appropriate error message and exits with a non-zero exit code.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/validate-yaml.ts`:21-22 - `else if (error.code === \"EACCES\") { process.stderr.write(\"Error: Cannot read file: ${filePath}\\n\"); }`\n- Evidence: Functional test with a chmod 000 file outputs \"Error: Cannot read file: /tmp/test_noperm.yaml\" and exits with code 2. The EACCES error code is properly handled and distinct from the ENOENT branch.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-003: YAML Syntax Validation\n**AC-003.1**: Valid YAML files containing key-value pairs are correctly identified as valid.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/yaml-parser.ts`:52-56 - `isValidLineContent()` checks for `: ` (colon-space) pattern in key-value pairs\n- Evidence: Parser unit tests at `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/yaml-parser.test.ts`:24-32 verify \"simple key-value\" (`name: John`) and \"multiple key-values\" (`name: John\\nage: 30`) both return `{ valid: true }`. All tests pass.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-003.2**: Valid YAML files containing simple lists (dash-prefixed items) are correctly identified as valid.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/yaml-parser.ts`:43-45 - `isValidLineContent()` checks for `- ` (dash-space) prefix or bare `-`\n- Evidence: Parser unit test at `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/yaml-parser.test.ts`:34-37 verifies \"simple list\" (`- item1\\n- item2`) returns `{ valid: true }`. Bare list item test (lines 109-112) also passes.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-003.3**: Valid YAML files containing nested structures (indented keys/values) are correctly identified as valid.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/yaml-parser.ts`:104,130-158 - Indentation stack logic with `indentStack` array handles nesting via push/pop\n- Evidence: Parser unit tests verify \"nested mapping\" (`parent:\\n  child: value`), \"nested list under key\" (`items:\\n  - one\\n  - two`), \"deep nesting\" (`a:\\n  b:\\n    c: d`), and \"list under nested key\" (`root:\\n  items:\\n    - one\\n    - two`). All return `{ valid: true }` and pass.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-003.4**: Files with inconsistent indentation levels within the same block are identified as invalid.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/yaml-parser.ts`:145-157 - Dedent logic pops the indent stack and returns error if no matching level found; lines 134-143 check `prevAllowsNesting` guard\n- Evidence: Parser unit tests verify \"inconsistent indentation\" (`a:\\n  b: 1\\n   c: 2`) returns `{ valid: false }` with error message containing \"indentation\" at line 3. \"Dedent to invalid level\" test also passes correctly.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-003.5**: Files with invalid key-value syntax (e.g., missing colon separator) are identified as invalid.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/yaml-parser.ts`:163-171 - `isValidLineContent()` returns false for lines that are neither key-value pairs nor list items, triggering syntax error\n- Evidence: Parser unit test \"missing colon (bare words)\" verifies `parseYaml(\"not a valid line\")` returns `{ valid: false }` with error containing \"syntax\" at line 1. \"Bare word on second line\" test also passes.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-003.6**: Files containing only comments and/or blank lines are treated as valid (empty document).\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/yaml-parser.ts`:111-117 - Blank lines (`.trim().length === 0`) and comment-only lines (`.trimStart().startsWith(\"#\")`) are skipped via `continue`\n- Evidence: Parser unit tests \"comment-only file\" (`# comment\\n# another`), \"whitespace-only file\" (`  \\n  \\n`), and \"comments with leading whitespace\" all return `{ valid: true }`. Functional test also confirmed comment-only file.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-003.7**: An empty file (zero bytes) is treated as valid.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/yaml-parser.ts`:99-101 - `if (content.length === 0 || content.trim().length === 0) return { valid: true }`\n- Evidence: Parser unit test \"empty file\" verifies `parseYaml(\"\")` returns `{ valid: true }`. CLI integration test \"empty file outputs valid and exits with code 0\" also passes. Functional test with touch-created empty file confirmed.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-004: Pass/Fail Output\n**AC-004.1**: On a valid file, the command outputs a message to stdout indicating the file is valid.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/validate-yaml.ts`:32 - `process.stdout.write(\"${filePath} is valid\\n\")`\n- Evidence: Functional test shows output: \"/tmp/test_valid.yaml is valid\" written to stdout. CLI integration test verifies stdout contains \"valid\".\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-004.2**: On an invalid file, the command outputs a message to stderr indicating the file is invalid, including a brief description of the error encountered.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/validate-yaml.ts`:35-37 - `process.stderr.write(\"${filePath} is invalid: ${result.error!.message} (line ${result.error!.line})\\n\")`\n- Evidence: Functional test shows output: \"/tmp/test_invalid.yaml is invalid: Invalid syntax: expected key-value pair or list item (line 1)\" written to stderr. The message includes the error description and line number.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-004.3**: Output messages include the file path so the user can confirm which file was validated.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/validate-yaml.ts`:32,35-37 - Both valid and invalid output messages use `${filePath}` as a prefix\n- Evidence: Valid output: \"/tmp/test_valid.yaml is valid\" (includes path). Invalid output: \"/tmp/test_invalid.yaml is invalid: ...\" (includes path). Both cases confirmed via functional testing.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-005: Exit Code Convention\n**AC-005.1**: Exit code 0 is returned when the YAML file is valid.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/validate-yaml.ts`:33 - `process.exit(0)`\n- Evidence: Functional test confirmed exit code 0 for valid YAML files. CLI integration tests also verify exit code 0 for valid and empty files.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-005.2**: A non-zero exit code (1) is returned when the YAML file has syntax errors.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/validate-yaml.ts`:38 - `process.exit(1)` in the `else` branch when `result.valid` is false\n- Evidence: Functional test confirmed exit code 1 for invalid YAML file. CLI integration test at line 64 verifies `exitCode` is 1 for invalid YAML.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-005.3**: A non-zero exit code (2) is returned for operational errors (file not found, file not readable, missing argument).\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/53f53ddd/workspace/src/validate-yaml.ts`:9,26 - `process.exit(2)` in the no-argument branch and in all file-read error branches\n- Evidence: Functional tests confirmed exit code 2 for: (1) no arguments, (2) file not found, (3) file not readable (permissions). CLI integration tests also verify code 2 for missing args and nonexistent file.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-006: Comment Handling\n**AC-006.1**: Lines consist