        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 5 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 2.5 days\n**Started**: 2026-03-02\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd a `validate-yaml` subcommand to the CLI tool that accepts a YAML file path, validates its syntactic correctness using a hand-written validator (no external dependencies), and outputs a clear pass/fail result with actionable error messages and appropriate exit codes for CI/CD integration.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1, T2] - Command routing structure and core validator logic are independent; T1 defines dispatch, T2 defines pure validation function\n2. [T3] - Tests require T2's exported interface to import and test against\n3. [T4] - Integration requires both T1 (routing) and T2 (validator) to be in place\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T3 -> T2 (Interface: tests import `validateYaml` and types from `yaml-validator.ts`)\n- T4 -> T1 (Build: integration wires into the routing structure defined by T1)\n- T4 -> T2 (Build: integration calls `validateYamlFile` defined by T2)\n\n**Critical Path**: T2 -> T3 -> T4\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Command Routing and Core Validator (Parallel Group 1)\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Add command dispatch logic to `src/index.ts` entry point `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-module-srcindexts-modified](design.md#33-module-srcindexts-modified)\n\n    **Effort**: 1 hour\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `src/index.ts` contains a switch/conditional on `process.argv[2]` that routes `\"validate-yaml\"` to the validator handler\n    - [ ] When `process.argv[2]` is not a known command, existing greeting behavior is preserved (backward compatibility)\n    - [ ] When `validate-yaml` is invoked without a file path argument, a usage help message is printed to stderr and the process exits with code 1\n    - [ ] Usage help message matches the format specified in design.md section 3.5\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement YAML validator core module with `validateYaml`, `validateYamlFile`, `formatValidationError`, and supporting types `[complexity:complex]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-data-types](design.md#31-data-types), [design.md#32-module-srcyaml-validatorts](design.md#32-module-srcyaml-validatorts)\n\n    **Effort**: 10 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `src/yaml-validator.ts` exports `ValidationResult` and `ValidationError` interfaces matching the design specification\n    - [ ] `validateYaml(content: string)` is a pure function that returns a `ValidationResult`\n    - [ ] Validator correctly handles indentation validation (spaces only, no tabs; consistent indentation levels)\n    - [ ] Validator correctly handles key-value mapping syntax (`key: value`, detection of missing colons)\n    - [ ] Validator correctly handles sequence/list syntax (`- item`, consistent indentation)\n    - [ ] Validator skips comment lines (lines starting with `#` after optional whitespace)\n    - [ ] Validator handles quoted strings (single and double quotes, balanced detection)\n    - [ ] Validator recognizes multi-line scalar indicators (`|` and `>`)\n    - [ ] Validator treats empty documents as valid (per BR-002)\n    - [ ] Validator recognizes document markers (`---` and `...`)\n    - [ ] `validateYamlFile(filePath: string)` reads a file using `Bun.file()` API and delegates to `validateYaml`\n    - [ ] `validateYamlFile` returns a `ValidationResult` with a file-not-found error when the file does not exist\n    - [ ] `validateYamlFile` catches I/O errors (permission denied, etc.) and returns them as `ValidationResult` errors\n    - [ ] `formatValidationError(error: ValidationError)` returns a formatted string including line number, optional column, and message\n    - [ ] No new dependencies are added to `package.json` (FR-004 / AC-004a)\n\n### Tests (Group 2)\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Create comprehensive test suite for YAML validator in `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 5 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Tests use `bun:test` framework, following existing project test patterns\n    - [ ] `validateYaml` valid YAML cases: empty string, simple key-value, nested mappings, sequences, mixed mappings and sequences, comments, quoted strings, multi-line scalars (`|`, `>`), document markers (`---`, `...`), boolean/null/numeric values\n    - [ ] `validateYaml` invalid YAML cases: tab indentation (error with line number), inconsistent indentation (error with line number), unclosed quoted string (error with line number), mapping without colon (error with line number)\n    - [ ] `validateYaml` edge cases: file with only comments returns valid, file with only whitespace returns valid, single scalar value returns valid\n    - [ ] `validateYamlFile` tests: valid file with valid YAML returns valid, non-existent file returns file-not-found error, valid file with invalid YAML returns errors with details\n    - [ ] `formatValidationError` tests: formats error with line number and message, formats error with line number, column, and message\n    - [ ] All tests pass via `bun test`\n\n### CLI Integration (Group 3)\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Wire `validateYamlFile` into command router with output formatting and exit codes `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#34-exit-code-strategy](design.md#34-exit-code-strategy), [design.md#35-output-format](design.md#35-output-format)\n\n    **Effort**: 4 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Valid YAML file produces stdout message in format `{filename}: Valid YAML` and exits with code 0 (AC-001a, AC-003a)\n    - [ ] Invalid YAML file produces stderr output with `{filename}: Invalid YAML` followed by indented error details with line numbers and exits with code 1 (AC-001b, AC-002a, AC-002b, AC-003b)\n    - [ ] File not found produces stderr message in format `Error: File not found: {path}` and exits with code 1 (AC-001c, AC-003c)\n    - [ ] File read errors (permissions, etc.) produce stderr error message and exit with code 1 (AC-003c)\n    - [ ] Success messages go to stdout, error messages go to stderr (design section 3.4)\n    - [ ] Output format matches design.md section 3.5 specifications exactly\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Update README.md - Scripts / Structure `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: Scripts / Structure\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] README.md Scripts section documents the `validate-yaml` command usage including syntax and examples\n    - [ ] README.md Structure section lists the new `src/yaml-validator.ts` and `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` files\n    - [ ] Section reflects the current implementation accurately\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\n- [ ] AC-001a: When given a path to a file containing valid YAML, the command outputs a success message and exits with code 0\n- [ ] AC-001b: When given a path to a file containing invalid YAML, the command outputs an error message describing the syntax issue and exits with a non-zero exit code\n- [ ] AC-001c: When given a path to a file that does not exist, the command outputs a clear \"file not found\" error and exits with a non-zero exit code\n- [ ] AC-002a: The error message includes a human-readable description of what syntax rule was violated\n- [ ] AC-002b: Where determinable, the error message includes the approximate line number or position of the error\n- [ ] AC-003a: Exit code is 0 when the provided YAML file is syntactically valid\n- [ ] AC-003b: Exit code is 1 (or another non-zero value) when the provided YAML file is syntactically invalid\n- [ ] AC-003c: Exit code is non