s using `formatValidationError`, all via `console.error`, then calls `process.exit(1)`. Integration test confirmed: invalid YAML file produces error message with line number and exits with code 1.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-001c**: When given a path to a file that does not exist, the command outputs a clear \"file not found\" error and exits with a non-zero exit code.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/cd7c5e8c/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/yaml-validator.ts`:170-176 - validateYamlFile file existence check; `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/cd7c5e8c/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/index.ts`:33-37 - I/O error output path\n- Evidence: validateYamlFile checks `await file.exists()` and returns `{ valid: false, errors: [{ line: 0, message: \"File not found: ...\" }] }`. index.ts detects I/O errors (line === 0) and outputs `Error: ${error.message}` to stderr, then exits with code 1. Integration test confirmed: `Error: File not found: /tmp/nonexistent_file.yaml` with exit code 1.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-002: Display Meaningful Error Messages\n\n**AC-002a**: The error message includes a human-readable description of what syntax rule was violated.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/cd7c5e8c/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/yaml-validator.ts`:77-83 (tab errors), 97-101 (unclosed quotes), 88-93 (flow collection errors), 153-156 (generic syntax errors)\n- Evidence: Each error type produces a descriptive message: \"Tab character found; YAML requires spaces for indentation\", \"Unclosed quoted string\", \"Unmatched opening brace '{'\", \"Unmatched closing bracket ']'\", \"Invalid YAML syntax\". Integration test confirmed descriptive messages are displayed.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-002b**: Where determinable, the error message includes the approximate line number or position of the error.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/cd7c5e8c/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/yaml-validator.ts`:33 (lineNum = i + 1), all error pushes include `line: lineNum`; `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/cd7c5e8c/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/yaml-validator.ts`:12-17 - formatValidationError\n- Evidence: All errors include 1-based line numbers. Tab errors additionally include column numbers (line 79: `column: (tabMatch.index ?? 0) + 1`). The `formatValidationError` function at lines 12-17 outputs `Line {N}: {message}` or `Line {N}, Column {C}: {message}` format. Integration test confirmed: \"Line 2, Column 1: Tab character found...\" and \"Line 1: Unclosed quoted string\".\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-003: Exit Codes for Scripting\n\n**AC-003a**: Exit code is 0 when the provided YAML file is syntactically valid.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/cd7c5e8c/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/index.ts`:31 - `process.exit(0)`\n- Evidence: Line 31 of index.ts explicitly calls `process.exit(0)` when `result.valid` is true. Integration test confirmed exit code 0 for valid YAML files (including empty files).\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-003b**: Exit code is 1 (or another non-zero value) when the provided YAML file is syntactically invalid.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/cd7c5e8c/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/index.ts`:44 - `process.exit(1)`\n- Evidence: Line 44 of index.ts calls `process.exit(1)` for all invalid YAML cases (both syntax errors and I/O errors). Integration test confirmed exit code 1 for invalid YAML files.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-003c**: Exit code is non-zero when the file cannot be read (missing file, permission error, etc.).\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/cd7c5e8c/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/yaml-validator.ts`:170-176 (file not found), 179-186 (catch block for I/O errors); `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/cd7c5e8c/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/index.ts`:33-37, 44 (error output and exit code 1)\n- Evidence: validateYamlFile handles both file-not-found (explicit existence check) and general I/O errors (try-catch) by returning `{ valid: false, errors: [...] }` with line 0 and descriptive messages. index.ts routes these to stderr and exits with code 1. Integration test confirmed exit code 1 for non-existent file.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-004: No New Dependencies\n\n**AC-004a**: After implementation, the dependencies and devDependencies fields in package.json contain no new entries compared to before the feature was added.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/cd7c5e8c/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/package.json`\n- Evidence: The package.json in the worktree is byte-for-byte identical to the original on the main branch. Both contain only `\"devDependencies\": { \"@types/bun\": \"latest\" }` and no `dependencies` field. The YAML validator is entirely hand-written using only TypeScript and the Bun runtime API (`Bun.file()`).\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### FR-005: Usage Help\n\n**AC-005a**: Invoking the YAML validate command with no arguments prints a usage hint to the console.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/cd7c5e8c/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/index.ts`:13-27 - usage help block\n- Evidence: Lines 13-27 of index.ts check if `filePath` is falsy and output a comprehensive usage message via `console.error` that includes the command syntax, description, arguments section, and exit codes. The message matches the format specified in design.md section 3.5. Integration test confirmed the full usage message is displayed when running `bun run dev validate-yaml` with no file path argument, with exit code 1.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n## Implementation Gap Analysis\n\n### Missing Implementations\nNone. All 10 acceptance criteria from requirements are fully implemented.\n\n### Partial Implementations\nNone.\n\n### Implementation Issues\nNone identified.\n\n### Notes on \"Could Have\" Features\n- **AC-006a** (stdin support, FR-006, Priority: Could Have): Not implemented. This is expected as it was classified as \"Could Have\" priority and was not part of the core implementation tasks. This is not considered a gap.\n\n## Code Quality Assessment\n\n**Overall Quality: HIGH**\n\n1. **Architecture**: Clean separation of concerns following the design. Pure function `validateYaml` handles syntax validation logic with no side effects. I/O wrapper `validateYamlFile` handles file system operations. Entry point `index.ts` handles CLI routing, output formatting, and exit codes. This matches the design's D3 decision (pure function core with I/O wrapper).\n\n2. **Type Safety**: Properly defined TypeScript interfaces (`ValidationResult`, `ValidationError`) matching the design specification exactly. All functions have explicit type signatures.\n\n3. **Error Handling**: Comprehensive error handling at multiple levels:\n   - File existence check before read attempt\n   - Try-catch for unexpected I/O errors (permissions, etc.)\n   - Per-line syntax error detection with descriptive messages\n   - Proper error routing in index.ts (line 0 = I/O error, line > 0 = syntax error)\n\n4. **Test Coverage**: 37 dedicated tests across 3 describe blocks covering:\n   - 16 valid YAML cases (including edge cases like empty files, comments-only, whitespace-only, flow collections)\n   - 6 invalid YAML cases (tabs, unclosed quotes, unmatched braces/brackets)\n   - 11 edge cases (block scalars, inline comments, Windows line endings)\n   - 3 file I/O tests (valid file, missing file, invalid content)\n   - 2 formatting tests\n   - All 39 tests (37 new + 2 existing) pass in 15ms\n\n5. **Backward Compatibility**: The default case in the switch statement preserves existing greeting behavior (`const name = command ?? \"World\"`). Existing tests in `utils.test.ts` continue to pass.\n\n6. **Code Organization**: Follows existing project patterns - source in `src/`, co-located test file with `.test.ts` suffix, `bun:test` framework.\n\n7. **Documentation**: README.md updated with comprehensive usage documentation including command syntax, arguments, exit codes, examples, and sample output. Project structure section updated to list new files.\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. No blocking issues found. The implementation is complete and ready for merge.\n\n2. For future enhancement, consider implementing AC-006a (stdin support) as a follow-up feature, as it would enable pipeline usage like `cat config.yaml | bun run dev validate-yaml`.\n\n3. Consider adding a few additional invalid YAML test cases for edge scenarios such as: duplicate keys at the same mapping level (noted as \"if detectable\" in the test plan), and deeply nested indentation validation.\n\n4. The \"Invalid YAML syntax\" generic fallback message (yaml-validator.ts:156) could be made more specific in future iterations to help users understand exactly what went wrong when the line does not match any recognized YAML construct.\n\n## Verification Evidence\n\n### Integration Test Results\n\n**Valid YAML file:**\n```\n$ bun run dev validate-yaml /tmp/test_valid.yaml\n/tmp/test_valid.yaml: Valid YAML\nExit code: 0\n```\n\n**Invalid YAML file (unclosed quote):**\n```\n$ bun run dev validate-yaml /tmp/test_invalid.yaml\n/tmp/test_invalid.yaml: Invalid YAML\n  Line 1: Unclosed quoted string\nExit code: 1\n```\n\n**Invalid YAML file (tab indentation):**\n```\n$ bun run dev validate-yaml /tmp/test_tab.yaml\n/tmp/test_tab.yaml: Invalid YAML\n  Line 2, Column 1: Tab character found; YAML requires spaces for indentation\nExit code: 1\n```\n\n**Non-existent file:**\n```\n$ bun run dev validate-yaml /tmp/nonexistent_file.yaml\nError: File not found: /tmp/nonexistent_file.yaml\nExit code: 1\n```\n\n**No arguments (usage help):**\n```\n$ bun run dev validate-yaml\nUsage: bun run dev validate-yaml <file-path>\n\nValidates a YAML file for syntactic correctness.\n\nArguments:\n  file-path    Path to the YAML file to validate\n\nExit codes:\n  0    YAML is valid\n  1    YAML is invalid or an error occurred\nExit code: 1\n```\n\n**Empty file (BR-002 compliance):**\n```\n$ bun run dev validate-yaml /tmp/test_empty.yaml\n/tmp/test_empty.yaml: Valid YAML\nExit code: 0\n```\n\n**Backward compatibility (greeting still works):**\n```\n$ bun run dev Alice\nHello, Alice!\nExit code: 0\n```\n\n### Test Suite Results\n\n```\nbun test v1.3.3\n 39 pass\n  0 fail\n 87 expect() calls\nRan 39 tests across 2 files. [15.00ms]\n```\n\n### Dependency Verification\n\nOriginal package.json (main branch) and current package.json are identical. No new dependencies or devDependencies added.\n\n### Key Code References\n\n- Command router: `src/index.ts` lines 10-52 (switch on process.argv[2])\n- Usage help: `src/index.ts` lines 14-24\n- Valid YAML output: `src/index.ts` lines 29-31\n- Invalid YAML output: `src/index.ts` lines 38-43\n- I/O error output: `src/index.ts` lines 34-37\n- ValidationResult/ValidationError types: `src/yaml-validator.ts` lines 1-10\n- formatValidationError: `src/yaml-validator.ts` lines 12-17\n- validateYaml (core logic): `src/yaml-validator.ts` lines 19-163\n- validateYamlFile (I/O wrapper): `src/yaml-validator.ts` lines 165-187\n- Test suite: `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` lines 1-367 (37 tests)\n"
