        "content": "# Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Created**: 2026-03-02\n**Status**: Draft\n\n---\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThis feature adds a `validate-yaml` subcommand to the existing CLI tool. The command accepts a YAML file path, reads the file, validates its syntactic correctness using a hand-written YAML syntax validator (no external dependencies), and outputs a clear pass/fail result with actionable error messages. Exit codes are set appropriately for CI/CD integration.\n\nThe design follows the existing project patterns: pure utility functions in dedicated modules, co-located tests using `bun:test`, and argument handling via `process.argv`.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    A[User / CI Pipeline] -->|\"bun run dev validate-yaml file.yaml\"| B[src/index.ts<br/>Command Router]\n    B -->|\"validate-yaml\"| C[src/yaml-validator.ts<br/>validateYamlFile]\n    B -->|\"default\"| D[src/utils.ts<br/>greet]\n    C -->|\"reads\"| E[Filesystem<br/>YAML File]\n    C -->|\"calls\"| F[validateYaml<br/>Core Validator]\n    F -->|\"returns\"| G[ValidationResult]\n    G -->|\"formats\"| H[Console Output<br/>+ Exit Code]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### Component Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"Entry Point\"\n        IDX[src/index.ts<br/>Command Router]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"YAML Validator Module\"\n        VF[validateYamlFile<br/>File I/O + orchestration]\n        VY[validateYaml<br/>Pure syntax validation]\n        FMT[formatValidationError<br/>Error message formatting]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Existing Module\"\n        UTL[src/utils.ts<br/>greet, add]\n    end\n\n    IDX -->|\"argv[2] === 'validate-yaml'\"| VF\n    IDX -->|\"default greeting\"| UTL\n    VF -->|\"reads file, passes content\"| VY\n    VY -->|\"returns ValidationResult\"| VF\n    VF -->|\"on error\"| FMT\n    FMT -->|\"formatted string\"| VF\n    VF -->|\"console.log/error + process.exit\"| IDX\n```\n\n### Command Flow Sequence\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant index.ts\n    participant yaml-validator.ts\n    participant Filesystem\n\n    User->>index.ts: bun run dev validate-yaml path/to/file.yaml\n    index.ts->>index.ts: Parse argv: command=\"validate-yaml\", filePath=\"path/to/file.yaml\"\n\n    alt No file path provided\n        index.ts->>User: Print usage help, exit(1)\n    end\n\n    index.ts->>yaml-validator.ts: validateYamlFile(filePath)\n    yaml-validator.ts->>Filesystem: Bun.file(filePath).text()\n\n    alt File not found / read error\n        Filesystem-->>yaml-validator.ts: Error\n        yaml-validator.ts-->>index.ts: { valid: false, error: \"File not found: ...\" }\n        index.ts->>User: Print error, exit(1)\n    end\n\n    Filesystem-->>yaml-validator.ts: fileContent\n    yaml-validator.ts->>yaml-validator.ts: validateYaml(fileContent)\n\n    alt Valid YAML\n        yaml-validator.ts-->>index.ts: { valid: true }\n        index.ts->>User: Print success message, exit(0)\n    else Invalid YAML\n        yaml-validator.ts-->>index.ts: { valid: false, errors: [...] }\n        index.ts->>User: Print formatted errors, exit(1)\n    end\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 Data Types\n\n```typescript\n/** Result of validating a YAML string */\nexport interface ValidationResult {\n  valid: boolean;\n  errors: ValidationError[];\n}\n\n/** A single validation error */\nexport interface ValidationError {\n  line: number;        // 1-based line number\n  column?: number;     // 1-based column (where determinable)\n  message: string;     // Human-readable error description\n}\n```\n\n### 3.2 Module: `src/yaml-validator.ts`\n\n**Exported Functions:**\n\n| Function | Signature | Purpose |\n|----------|-----------|---------|\n| `validateYaml` | `(content: string) => ValidationResult` | Pure function: validates YAML syntax from a string |\n| `validateYamlFile` | `(filePath: string) => Promise<ValidationResult>` | Reads file and delegates to `validateYaml`; handles I/O errors |\n| `formatValidationError` | `(error: ValidationError) => string` | Formats a single error for console output |\n\n**`validateYaml` Implementation Strategy:**\n\nThe validator processes YAML content line by line, maintaining a parse state to detect syntax errors. It handles:\n\n1. **Indentation validation**: Consistent use of spaces (no tabs), consistent indentation levels within a block\n2. **Key-value mapping syntax**: Proper `key: value` structure, detection of missing colons\n3. **Sequence (list) syntax**: Proper `- item` structure, consistent indentation\n4. **Comments**: Lines starting with `#` (after optional whitespace) are skipped\n5. **Quoted strings**: Balanced single and double quotes, basic escape handling\n6. **Multi-line scalars**: Recognition of `|` and `>` block scalar indicators\n7. **Empty documents**: Treated as valid (per BR-002)\n8. **Document markers**: `---` and `...` recognized\n\n**Known Limitations (documented, not adding deps per BR-003):**\n\n- Does not validate complex YAML features like anchors/aliases (`&`, `*`), tags (`!!`), or merge keys (`<<`)\n- Does not perform full YAML 1.2 spec type resolution\n- Flow-style collections (`{key: value}`, `[item1, item2]`) receive basic validation only\n- Does not validate character encoding beyond what Bun's file reader handles\n\n**`validateYamlFile` Implementation Strategy:**\n\n1. Check file existence using `Bun.file(filePath).exists()`\n2. Read content using `Bun.file(filePath).text()`\n3. Catch I/O errors (permission denied, etc.) and return as `ValidationResult` with appropriate error\n4. Delegate to `validateYaml(content)` for syntax validation\n\n### 3.3 Module: `src/index.ts` (Modified)\n\nThe entry point gains a simple command router:\n\n```typescript\nconst command = process.argv[2];\n\nswitch (command) {\n  case \"validate-yaml\": {\n    const filePath = process.argv[3];\n    if (!filePath) {\n      console.error(\"Usage: bun run dev validate-yaml <file-path>\");\n      process.exit(1);\n    }\n    // call validateYamlFile, output results, set exit code\n    break;\n  }\n  default: {\n    // Existing greeting behavior (backward compatible)\n    const name = command ?? \"World\";\n    console.log(greet(name));\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis preserves backward compatibility: any argument that is not a known command is treated as a name for the greeting (existing behavior).\n\n### 3.4 Exit Code Strategy\n\n| Scenario | Exit Code | Output Stream |\n|----------|-----------|---------------|\n| Valid YAML | 0 | stdout: success message |\n| Invalid YAML (syntax error) | 1 | stderr: error details |\n| File not found | 1 | stderr: file not found message |\n| File read error (permissions, etc.) | 1 | stderr: error message |\n| Missing file path argument | 1 | stderr: usage help |\n\n### 3.5 Output Format\n\n**Success:**\n```\nfile.yaml: Valid YAML\n```\n\n**Error (syntax):**\n```\nfile.yaml: Invalid YAML\n  Line 5: Unexpected indentation level (expected 2 spaces, found 3)\n  Line 12: Missing value after colon in mapping\n```\n\n**Error (file not found):**\n```\nError: File not found: path/to/missing.yaml\n```\n\n**Usage help:**\n```\nUsage: bun run dev validate-yaml <file-path>\n\nValidates a YAML file for syntactic correctness.\n\nArguments:\n  file-path    Path to the YAML file to validate\n\nExit codes:\n  0    YAML is valid\n  1    YAML is invalid or an error occurred\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology | Rationale |\n|-------|-----------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Existing project runtime |\n| Language | TypeScript (strict) | Existing project language |\n| File I/O | `Bun.file()` API | Bun-native file reading, async, no deps |\n| Testing | `bun:test` | Existing test framework |\n| YAML Parsing | Hand-written validator | FR-004 constraint: no new dependencies |\n\nNo changes to `package.json` dependencies or devDependencies.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| ID | Component | Description | Files |\n|----|-----------|-------------|-------|\n| T1 | Command Router | Add command dispatch logic to entry point | `src/index.ts` |\n| T2 | YAML Validator Core | Implement `validateYaml`, `formatValidationError`, types | `src/yaml-validator.ts` |\n| T3 | YAML Validator Tests | Comprehensive test suite for validator | `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` |\n| T4 | CLI Integration | Wire `validateYamlFile` into command router, handle I/O, exit codes | `src/index.ts`, `src/yaml-validator.ts` |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1, T2] - Command routing structure and core validator logic are independent; T1 defines dispatch, T2 defines pure validation function\n2. [T3] - Tests require T2's exported interface to import and test against\n3. [T4] - Integration requires both T1 (routing) and T2 (validator) to be in place\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T3 -> T2 (Interface: tests import `validateYaml` and types from `yaml-validator.ts`)\n- T4 -> T1 (Build: integration wires into the routing structure defined by T1)\n- T4 -> T2 (Build: integration calls `validateYamlFile` defined by T2)\n\n**Critical Path**: T2 -> T3 -> T4\n\n---\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### Test Value Assessment\n\n| Test Category | Value | Rationale |\n|---------------|-------|-----------|\n| `validateYaml` with valid YAML inputs | HIGH - design for | Core business logic: does the validator correctly accept valid YAML? |\n| `validateYaml` with invalid YAML inputs | HIGH - design for | Core business logic: does the validator correctly reject and report errors? |\n| Error message quality (line numbers, descriptions) | HIGH - design for | App-specific error handling: are errors actionable? |\n| `validateYamlFile` with missing file | HIGH - design for | App-specific error handling: file-not-found case |\n| `validateYaml` with empty input | MEDIUM - design for | Business rule BR-002: empty documents are valid |\n| Command routing dispatch | MEDIUM - design for | Integration: correct command reaches correct handler |\n| Exit code verification | LOW - do NOT design unit tests for | Framework behavior (`process.exit`); covered by integration/manual testing |\n| Bun.file() read behavior | AVOID | Library behavior verification; trust the runtime |\n\n### Test Plan\n\n**File: `src/yaml-validator.test.ts`**\n\n```\ndescribe(\"validateYaml\")\n  -- Valid YAML cases --\n  test: empty string returns valid\n  test: simple key-value pair returns valid\n  test: nested mappings return valid\n  test: sequences (lists) return valid\n  test: mixed mappings and sequences return valid\n  test: comments are ignored and document is valid\n  test: quoted strings (single and double) return valid\n  test: multi-line scalars (| and >) return valid\n  test: document markers (--- and ...) return valid\n  test: boolean, null, numeric values return valid\n\n  -- Invalid YAML cases --\n  test: tab indentation returns error with line number\n  test: inconsistent indentation returns error with line number\n  test: unclosed quoted string returns error with line number\n  test: mapping without colon returns error with line number\n  test: duplicate keys at same level returns error (if detectable)\n  test: invalid characters return error with line number\n\n  -- Edge cases --\n  test: file with only comments returns valid\n  test: file with only whitespace returns valid\n  test: single scalar value returns valid\n\ndescribe(\"validateYamlFile\")\n  test: valid file path with valid YAML returns valid result\n  test: non-existent file path returns error result with file-not-found message\n  test: valid file path with invalid YAML returns errors with details\n\ndescribe(\"formatValidationError\")\n  test: formats error with line number and message\n  test: formats error with line number, column, and message\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Deployment Design\n\nNo special deployment considerations. This feature adds new source files and modifies `src/index.ts`. The existing `bun run dev` script remains the entry point.\n\n| Aspect | Detail |\n|--------|--------|\n| Build | No build changes; Bun runs TypeScript directly |\n| Dependencies | No changes to `package.json` |\n| Configuration | None required |\n| Migration | None required |\n| Rollback | Revert the commit |\n\n---\n\n## 9. Documentation Impact\n\n| Type | Target | Section | KB Source | Rationale |\n|------|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| edit | README.md | Scripts / Structure | N/A | Add `validate-yaml` command usage and new file to structure listing |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Design Decisions Log\n\nSee `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/cd7c5e8c/workspace/.rp1/work/features/yaml-validator-command/design-decisions.md` for the full decisions log.\n\nKey decisions:\n- **D1**: Hand-written YAML validator over external library (FR-004 constraint)\n- **D2**: Subcommand pattern (`validate-yaml`) preserving backward compatibility\n- **D3**: Pure function core (`validateYaml`) with I/O wrapper (`validateYamlFile`) for testability\n- **D4**: Line-by-line validation approach for simplicity and error reporting\n- **D5**: Stderr for errors, stdout for success, consistent exit codes\n"
