        "old_string": "# rp1-eval-project\n\nA minimal Bun project for testing rp1 agent evaluations.\n\n## Scripts\n\n- `bun run dev` - Run the main entry point\n- `bun test` - Run tests\n- `bun run lint` - Run linter\n- `bun run format` - Run formatter\n\n## Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  index.ts    - Main entry point\n  utils.ts    - Utility functions\n```",
        "new_string": "# rp1-eval-project\n\nA minimal Bun project for testing rp1 agent evaluations.\n\n## Scripts\n\n- `bun run dev` - Run the main entry point (default: greeting)\n- `bun run dev validate-yaml <file-path>` - Validate a YAML file for syntactic correctness\n- `bun test` - Run tests\n- `bun run lint` - Run linter\n- `bun run format` - Run formatter\n\n### YAML Validator\n\nValidate YAML files for syntax errors directly from the command line.\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```bash\nbun run dev validate-yaml <file-path>\n```\n\n**Arguments:**\n\n- `file-path` - Path to the YAML file to validate\n\n**Exit codes:**\n\n- `0` - YAML is valid\n- `1` - YAML is invalid or an error occurred\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```bash\n# Validate a YAML configuration file\nbun run dev validate-yaml config.yaml\n\n# Use in a CI pipeline (fails the step if YAML is invalid)\nbun run dev validate-yaml deployment.yaml && echo \"YAML OK\"\n```\n\n**Output:**\n\n```\n# Valid file\nconfig.yaml: Valid YAML\n\n# Invalid file (syntax errors reported with line numbers)\nconfig.yaml: Invalid YAML\n  Line 5: Tab character found; YAML requires spaces for indentation\n  Line 12: Unclosed quoted string\n\n# Missing file\nError: File not found: missing.yaml\n```\n\n## Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  index.ts                - Main entry point and command router\n  utils.ts                - Utility functions\n  utils.test.ts           - Tests for utility functions\n  yaml-validator.ts       - YAML syntax validator (validateYaml, validateYamlFile, formatValidationError)\n  yaml-validator.test.ts  - Tests for YAML validator\n```"
